        },
        {
          "text": "The result is observed by value: its getKey() and getValue() Strings, compared with String.equals. A null result is its own observation.",
          "basis": "The brief's observation decision (llm-dlc/loops/example-targets-positive.md, P1, and the seed's observation_decision): reference identity is excluded on purpose, because the patch changes which class owns the cached tags. Tag is micrometer's interface; both revisions build their tags with Tag.of(String, String) from micrometer-core, the same dependency at both commits (1.2.0)."
        },
        {
          "text": "Class initialization runs as on the JVM, never removed: WebMvcTags's static initializer (its cached Tags and the two Pattern.compile calls) on both sides, before's switch-map class WebMvcTags$1 and HttpStatus.Series, and after's Outcome enum, whose constructor calls Tag.of(\"outcome\", name()) six times.",
